# The decoy half of the R5 fixture: `lib/util.hero` exists here, so compiling
# `lib/leaf.hero` directly resolves `use util` to it and checks clean — a
# program legal under both bases, whose meaning depends on which file you
# compile. `main.hero` reads the root's `util` (3); the leaf, compiled alone,
# reads `lib/util` (4). This is the shape panel 099's ergonomist built and the
# rule the sitting adopted knowing it; the row that pins it says so.
use util
use lib/leaf

function main()
    print(util.scale())
    print(leaf.scaled())
